.TH MKDIR 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
mkdir \- make directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkdir
.RB [ \-p ]
.I directory ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Mkdir
creates each named directory.
Without
.BR \-p ,
an existing name is an error.
.TP
.B \-p
Make missing intermediate directories as well, and accept an existing
directory as success.
.PP
A failed operand is reported; the remaining operands are attempted.
Directories use ProDOS names and attributes, not Unix ownership or modes.
For example:
.PP
.B mkdir \-p work/src
.SH FILES
/usr/man/MKDIR  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
rmdir(1), ls(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 if all operands succeed, 1 if any cannot be created, 2 for usage errors.
